<title>BELGIUM: Belgian money market supply raised in week.</title>
<headline>Belgian money market supply raised in week.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian central bank said</p>
<p>it added liquidity to the money market in the week to March 24</p>
<p>to offset a rise in notes in circulation.</p>
<p>(figures from the weekly statement in bln francs) -</p>
<p> Foreign currency reserves	   449.661 ( - 0.536)</p>
<p> Advances against pledged security  16.017 ( + 1.948)</p>
<p> Commercial bills			  2.667 ( + 0.000)</p>
<p> Securities portfolio		   23.818 ( - 0.004)</p>
<p> Money market interventions*	  98.933 ( + 2.252)</p>
<p> Bank notes in circulation	   457.563 ( + 1.792)</p>
<p>* comprises repurchase agreements and interbank loans</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
